# XSH dlclose()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# What an implementation unloads is left to it, so only the return value and the validity of a second handle
# are checked. A handle that is not valid is never passed (the result for it is not safe to provoke).

assertion  XSH.dlclose.001
anchor     functions/dlclose.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/dlclose.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       dlclose() of a valid handle (from dlopen(NULL)) returns 0.
test       t/001-close.c

assertion  XSH.dlclose.002
anchor     functions/dlclose.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/dlclose.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       With two handles for the object that defines getpid(), dlclose() of
           each returns 0, and the second handle still finds a working getpid()
           after the first is closed.
note       An object may not be removed while a handle for it is open.
test       t/002-twice.c
